sole in-neighbour in the window is 1574 (step_15).\n\nBut the timestamps run backwards at two points (each node has only 1\u20132 events, so bucket counts pin them down):\n\n| hop | time bucket |\n|---|---|\n| 303 \u2192 1409 | 47196\u201347495 (step_06, step_08) |\n| 1409 \u2192 960 | 47496\u201347795 (step_08, step_09) |\n| 960 \u2192 254 | **46896\u201347195** (step_09, step_10, step_14) \u2014 *before* 960 was reached |\n| 254 \u2192 1574 | **47796\u201348095** (step_11, step_13) |\n| 1574 \u2192 1293 | **47496\u201347795** (step_07, step_11, step_12) \u2014 *before* 1574 was reached |\n\nSo 1574 contacted 1293 (~47.5\u201347.8k) *before* receiving anything from 254 (~47.8\u201348.1k), and 960 contacted 254 (~46.9\u201347.2k) *before* being reached by 1409 (~47.5\u201347.8k). No time-respecting ordering exists, regardless of the 600-unit gap constraint. There is no alternative path to test (k=4 neighbourhood of 303 contains only 5 nodes; 1293 has exactly one in-neighbour), so the static connection is a pure ignore-time artifact.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_7bc8a9fd\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [303, 1409, 960, 254, 1574, 1293],\n  \"window\": [46296, 48695],\n  \"confidence\": 0.87,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"The unique static chain 303->1409->960->254->1574->1293 is not time-respecting: 960 sent to 254 (~46.9-47.2k) before being contacted by 1409 (~47.5-47.8k), and 1574 sent to 1293 (~47.5-47.8k) before receiving from 254 (~47.8-48.1k). Since 1293's only in-neighbour is 1574 and 1574's only in-neighbour is 254, no alternative ordering can repair the chain. The apparent connection is an artifact of ignoring time, not a genuine cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 20808, "total_output_tokens": 4621, "total_tokens": 25429, "total_latency_ms": 56947, "llm_calls": 5, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}